Issues I found by reading the code:

XSS risk (high): renderVaultGrid and filterVault insert doc.title, party names, and content via innerHTML without escaping. A title like <img src=x onerror=alert(1)> would execute. printDocument also writes raw text into HTML. Fix: escape HTML or use textContent.
Bug: filterVault doesn't hide the empty state, and it shows raw content without the \n cleanup that renderVaultGrid applies.
Bug: the Enforceability and Liability percentages never update after an audit.
Logic flaw: any issue at all yields "HIGH RISK DETECTED". There is no medium tier, though the badge markup implies one. The "limitation of liability" check is also bypassed just by the word "indemnify".
Minor: the "Delaware LLC" option label is hardcoded, so it's wrong for other jurisdictions. The party-b-type values differ from Party A's.
Minor: document.execCommand('copy') is deprecated, so prefer navigator.clipboard.writeText with the current code as a fallback.
Minor: the word count does not refresh when the user types in the editor.

Exit criteria: all T1-T11 pass, the XSS issue is fixed, and no high-severity bugs remain open
